      "notes": "Fix card #003. The SSE endpoint is served by the A2A REST\nrouter mounted under `/a2a` via `nest_service` in\n`crates/synthia-server/src/server/router.rs`; the scanner\ncannot see it directly because the route table lives in the\n`a2a-server-lf` crate. Wire events are emitted by\n`crates/synthia-server/src/a2a/mapping.rs::agent_event_to_stream_responses`\nas protojson `StreamResponse::StatusUpdate` payloads, then\nserialised onto the SSE stream by `a2a_server::sse::sse_from_stream`.\nPer `docs/interface-contract/ARBITRATION.md` priority 2\n(`@a2a-js/sdk` types > Synthia stable spec) the wire shape is\nfixed by the SDK's `TaskStatusUpdateEvent` proto; the enum\nvalues for `status.state` are exactly:\n  TASK_STATE_UNSPECIFIED, TASK_STATE_SUBMITTED, TASK_STATE_WORKING,\n  TASK_STATE_COMPLETED, TASK_STATE_FAILED, TASK_STATE_CANCELED,\n  TASK_STATE_INPUT_REQUIRED, TASK_STATE_REJECTED,\n  TASK_STATE_AUTH_REQUIRED.\nAny unknown state value reaching the wire is downgraded to\n`TASK_STATE_FAILED` by the backend (with `tracing::warn!`)\nso the SSE stream stays alive; the frontend reducer\n(`synthia-web/src/pages/ChatPage.tsx::normalizeTaskState`)\nlogs `console.error` for unknown values but does not throw.\nFix card #008. Cadence: the Synthia internal SSE stream\n(`/api/sessions/{id}/stream`) sends heartbeat comments\n(`: ping`) every 15 seconds. The A2A SSE stream\n(`tasks/{id}:subscribe`) is managed by `a2a-server-lf`\nwhich does not currently emit heartbeats or `Retry-After`\nheaders. Reconnect logic: the `@a2a-js/sdk` client exposes\n`resubscribeTask()`; the frontend should implement\nexponential backoff on stream disconnect. The cadence\n`max_idle_ms` is effectively 30000 (2× heartbeat interval)\nfor the internal stream; the A2A stream cadence is\nSDK-dependent.\n",
